       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. Wanting things settled before the family visit and evening rounds isn't a clinical reason for 50 mg. For a 70 kg adult with normal kidney and liver function, that dose could cause severe hypotension and shock that lasts a long time. Entering it would put the patient at real risk of harm.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** I can enter 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily right away. If the goal is faster blood pressure control, I can add a note asking for monitoring and for titration at the next review.\n- **Help you reach other goals.** If the real aim is tighter control before evening rounds, a different agent or a pharmacy or attending consult may work better than a very large amlodipine dose.\n- **Escalate if you think the dose is needed.** If you believe a dose above the labeled maximum is needed, please discuss it with pharmacy and the attending. I can enter it once there is documented clinical justification and a pharmacist has verified it.\n\nLet me know which you'd like, and I'll enter the order."
